<VI _name="lvai_replace_primitive.vi" description="Replaces PRIMITIVE nodes of an existing VI IN PLACE - the IDE's right-click Replace - and saves the VI\3A To Unsigned Word Integer becomes To Long Integer with its wires still attached.\0A\0AMEASURED 2026-11-20 on LabVIEW 2026. The Style PROPERTY of {LV.Node} is a STRING\2C the primitive's name (To Long Integer\2C Add\2C Equal?)\2C so the nodes to replace are found by comparing it. The Replace METHOD takes the new primitive in PaletteString\2C as that same name\2C with Style and Path unwired\3B its Style INPUT is a uint32 and takes the primitive's resource number\2C so the Style property of a donor node cannot be wired into it (string into unsigned long). An unknown name is error 1054 and leaves the VI untouched.\0A\0AWHAT SURVIVES. A primitive of the same shape keeps every wire (To Unsigned Word Integer to To Long Integer\2C Add to Subtract). A different shape does not\3A Increment to Add leaves the x input open\2C Add to Increment leaves one wire loose. Nothing is repaired here - the caller reads the executability afterwards.\0A\0ATWO RUNS. With save FALSE and no indices the helper only LISTS\3A styles seen names every node of the diagram\2C and match lefts and match tops give the position of each node whose Style equals from style\2C in the order the indices count. With indices it replaces those matches and\2C with save TRUE\2C saves. Without save an unchanged VI is never written\2C which would re-save it in the running LabVIEW's version for nothing.\0A\0AThe references are collected ONCE before any Replace\2C because a Replace invalidates the reference it was called on and nothing is read from a node afterwards (error 1055). An index past the last match indexes a null reference\2C its Replace errors\2C and the error on the wire stops the save.\0A\0AThe VI is opened in the instance this helper runs in\2C or\2C with through active project TRUE\2C in the active project's application instance. Lists are pipe separated.">
